# The confirmation dialog and the text field - the two containers that used to be drawn by hand.
#
# Watch the action row rather than the panel: exactly one button carries a fill and it is always
# the one the cursor is on. The dialog opens on Cancel deliberately, so the first frame shows the
# safe answer filled and "Reboot now" as an accent-labelled text button - then Right moves the
# fill across. That is the whole of how it says which answer A would press, and it is a fill
# rather than a pair of fills because the high-contrast palette has only one yellow to spend.

scene demo
scale 4
delay 200

tab settings
key down 12
key a
hold 700

# Radio actions: the row under the "Power" heading is Reboot, whose confirmation is destructive -
# the warning icon and the headline take the bad tone rather than the accent.
key down 1
key a
hold 1200
key right
hold 1200
key left
hold 1200

# The same panel on a palette with one accent and no held-back version of it. The buttons cannot
# be told apart by hue here, which is exactly why the fill moves instead of being shared.
theme contrast
hold 1600
theme light
hold 1600
